1. DEFINITIONS

"Licensor" means Masrur Ahmmed.
"Software" means CoSign, including its source code, object code, build files,
  tests, documentation, and any updates or patches the Licensor provides.
"Licensee" means the legal entity named in an Order Form that holds an active
  Subscription.
"Affiliate" means an entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common
  control with the Licensee, and that operates a platform named in the Order Form.
"Order Form" means the document signed or accepted by the Licensor and Licensee
  that identifies the Licensee, covered platforms, fees and Term.
"Subscription" means the Licensee's paid right to use the Software for a Term.
"Term" means the subscription period stated in the Order Form (initially twelve
  months) and each renewal.
"Authorized Environment" means systems owned or controlled by the Licensee or its
  Affiliates, or by a cloud provider acting solely on their behalf, used to
  operate the covered platforms.
"Modify" means to alter, patch, adapt, translate, port, extend, or create a
  derivative work of the Software, in whole or in part.
"Fork" means any copy of the Software, or of a Modified version, that is kept in
  a repository, package registry or other location accessible to anyone other
  than the Licensee's authorized personnel, or that is maintained as an
  independent line of development.
"Configuration" means setting the policy parameters, keys, address lists, price
  feeds and other options that the Software exposes for that purpose. Configuration
  is not Modification.

2. LICENSE GRANT

Subject to this License and payment of fees, the Licensor grants the Licensee,
for the Term, a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to:

(a) install and run the Software in Authorized Environments to guard withdrawals
    on the Licensee's and its Affiliates' covered platforms;
(b) make the copies necessary for that operation, including backup, disaster
    recovery, staging and test environments, held only in Authorized Environments;
(c) perform Configuration; and
(d) read and analyze the source code for internal security review, including by
    third-party auditors bound by written confidentiality obligations at least as
    protective as Section 9.

