Any attempted Modification, distribution or Fork in breach of this Section is void
and creates no license in the resulting work, which is owned by the Licensor to the
extent it incorporates the Software.

4. PATCHES AND SUPPORT

(a) During the Term the Licensor will provide updates and security patches to the
    Licensee as stated in the Order Form.
(b) The Licensee may apply patches and updates issued by the Licensor. The Licensee
    shall deploy any update the Licensor designates "Critical" within fourteen (14)
    days of release.
(c) The Licensee may request changes in writing. A change written by the Licensee
    may be used only if the Licensor approves it in writing, and the Licensor may
    attach conditions.
(d) The Licensee grants the Licensor a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide,
    royalty-free license to use any feedback, suggestion or approved contribution
    without obligation to the Licensee.

5. FEES AND TERM

(a) The Licensee shall pay the annual fee in the Order Form, in advance, within
    thirty (30) days of invoice. Fees are non-refundable except as this License
    states, and exclude taxes, which the Licensee shall bear.
(b) The Subscription renews automatically for successive twelve-month Terms unless
    either party gives written notice of non-renewal at least sixty (60) days before
    the Term ends.
(c) The Licensor may change fees for a renewal Term by written notice at least
    ninety (90) days before that Term begins.

6. OWNERSHIP

The Licensor and its licensors own all rights, title and interest in the Software,
including all intellectual property. No right is granted by implication, estoppel
or otherwise except as stated. No right to use the Licensor's names or trademarks
is granted. The Licensee owns its data, keys, configuration and audit logs.

7. LICENSEE RESPONSIBILITIES

The Software is a risk-control layer. It is effective only when deployed as
intended. The Licensee is solely responsible for: (a) making the CoSign signing key
a required signer on each guarded wallet; (b) operating the Software on
infrastructure, accounts, keys and personnel that are independent of the
Licensee's exchange systems; (c) the custody, backup and rotation of all keys,
including approver and price-feed keys; (d) the policies it configures; and (e)
its own security review, testing and regulatory compliance before and during use.

8. COMPLIANCE VERIFICATION

(a) The Licensee shall keep accurate records of where the Software is deployed and
    shall certify compliance in writing on request, not more than once per twelve
    months.
(b) On thirty (30) days' notice, and not more than once per twelve months, the
    Licensor may verify compliance through the Licensee's records or an
    independent auditor bound by confidentiality. Verification is limited to
    deployment locations, copies and use of the Software, and excludes customer
    data, private keys and transaction content. The Licensee shall bear the cost
    only if verification shows material non-compliance.

9. CONFIDENTIALITY AND VULNERABILITY DISCLOSURE

(a) The source code, non-public documentation and non-public vulnerability
    information are the Licensor's confidential information. The Licensee shall
    protect them with at least reasonable care and use them only as this License
    permits.
(b) The Licensee shall report any suspected vulnerability in the Software to the
    Licensor promptly and privately, using the contact in Section 14.
(c) The Licensee shall not publicly disclose a vulnerability until the Licensor
    has released a fix or ninety (90) days have passed since the report,
    whichever is first, except where earlier disclosure is required by law or is
    necessary to protect users from active exploitation.

