11. TERMINATION AND TRANSITION

(a) Either party may terminate on written notice if the other materially breaches
    this License and fails to cure within thirty (30) days of notice. The Licensor
    may terminate immediately on notice if the Licensee breaches Section 3 or
    Section 9(a), or fails to pay after a further ten (10) days' notice.
(b) On expiry or termination the licenses in Section 2 end and the Licensee shall
    delete all copies of the Software, except that:
    (i) for ninety (90) days (the "Transition Period") the Licensee may continue to
        operate its existing deployment solely to migrate guarded assets to
        another control arrangement, so that expiry never traps funds; and
    (ii) the Licensee keeps its own data, keys, configuration and audit logs.
    The Transition Period does not apply where the Licensor terminates for breach
    of Section 3(c), 3(d), 3(e) or 3(g).
(c) Sections 3, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13 and 14 survive termination.

12. EVALUATION

Any organization may, without a Subscription, read the source code and run the
Software in a non-production environment for up to thirty (30) days solely to
evaluate it, subject to Sections 3 and 9. Evaluation use may not guard live funds.

13. REPOSITORY VISIBILITY AND PLATFORM FEATURES

The Software may be hosted on a code-hosting platform that lets users view or fork
repositories. Visibility of the repository, and any platform feature or terms that
allow copying, do not grant any license under this License. A copy or Fork made
without the Licensor's written authorization is unlicensed beyond the Section 12
